A||||12||fiero56||Window Tinting||||10||
Z||000000||fiero56||10-02-2000||09:21 PM||||I have been kicking around the idea of tinting the windows on the Fiero for a few weeks. My main concern has been seeing all those old vans with the peeling, bubbly film on the glass, didn't want that happening to my Fiero. I decided to go ahead, and slap some tint on the windows anyway. I didn't know how dark the different percentages were, but figured 5% sounded a little too dark(this isn't my 'hood' cruiser), but 20% sounded a little light. I went with 20% anyway, put it on, and it looks great! It is a little on the light side, but isn't too bad. Next is tinting the rear glass. I will stay with 20% just to match, and keep the anal area cops happy. Dark windows on a dark car look really good. Plus, didn't take too long to install. Might take a few pictures, will have to see what happens.||||reg||10
Z||000001||DjKid||10-02-2000||10:16 PM||||cops cant' say anything to ya bout ya back windows. If ya lookin for legal tint.. go to walmart.. thats all they sale<P>------------------<BR>Ray - Blue 88 Coupe - <A HREF="http://blueknight.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank>My Blue Knight</A> - <A HREF="http://www.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank> Carolina Fieros</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sillhouette.com||10-02-2000||11:25 PM||||Carfull with your back window.  If you mean the quarter windows on the fastback GT.  The tint will not adhere well onto plastic plus the fact the engine heat escapes at a very close proximity to those windows will crack your tint.  Carfull not to use anything abrasive on those windows either.  They are plastic and rare to find.  <P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000003||007DOUG||10-03-2000||12:25 AM||||Here's a really cool look on my 86 SE. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Tintedse.jpg"> <P>All windows are 5%. There's a 5" strip of 5% on top/bottom of windshield, with the center of the windshield done in 20%. NEVER put 5% on on your winshield. Its impossible to see the front of your car at night. 20% is easy to see out of at night.<P>We have a state law of 35% all windows, and nothing lower than the ASC line.<P>BUT.....also check your local laws for "loopholes". I've got a written Dr. Rx for my windows. <P>------------------<BR>5 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top<BR>84 SE<BR>86 SE V6 153K<BR>2 86 GT's<BR>86 GT 3.4 Pearl White T-top<BR>2 88 GT's (twins)<P>However......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||10-03-2000||01:24 AM||||My tint was $99.00 for all 3 windows. Limo on the rear & Med. on the sides. The good thing about having a shop do it is that most places give you a lifetime warranty.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/a.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/f.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2d_00010aa3.gif">  <P><B>Website's<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>www.WS6Fiero.com</A><P>                  <A HREF="http://www.hazeperformance.com" TARGET=_blank>www.HazePerformance.com </A></B>||||reg||14
Z||000005||DjKid||10-03-2000||01:36 AM||||*writes down haze's tag number*<P>I'm planning on 2% on my rear window and 5% on the sides..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Ray - Blue 88 Coupe - <A HREF="http://blueknight.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank>My Blue Knight</A> - <A HREF="http://www.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank> Carolina Fieros</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||10-03-2000||02:03 AM||||This is just a helpful suggestion. But most police officers hate tinted windows because they cannot see into the car too well at night. They don't feel safe when they cannot see into the car. To aid in you not getting hassled for your tint, If you are stopped at night, As soon as you pull over and stop Turn on the interior lights. This will allow the officer to see into the vehicle better and make him feel safe. Which will be "brownie points" for you where he may actually let you go with a warning if your offense isn't too severe.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||fiero56||10-03-2000||08:25 AM||||Good suggstion, Oreif. This might be a first, but I actually considered what a cop will think with one of my vehicle modifications. I can't say I considered the law(I couldn't care less what c'vill law says), but I don't want a cop going overboard with a traffic stop because of my windows.<P>The rear glass I was talking about is the glass in back just behind the seats. I have notchback, so no fastback windows.<BR>Here's picture w/out tinting.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pffsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||fiero56||10-03-2000||02:56 PM||||I know this varies from city to city, but wonder if it is even worth looking into.<P>I wonder if it is legal to lightly tint the windshield, so it somewhat matches the rest of the glass on the car. Not looking to black anything out, but would be a nice change. Anyone have any thoughts on this?||||reg||1
Z||000009||DXR_DAD||10-03-2000||03:58 PM||||The less light you let in (by tinting) the darker the tint looks? My rear window is limo the darkest I could buy. At night my back window looks like it's painted Black! and the sides are darker than I would like (the cop thing)??? The sides look good in the day time<P>Just a thought????<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||5
Z||000010||zeusrekning||10-03-2000||04:26 PM||||djkid, the guy at the local tinting shop told me 22% was the limit on all vehicles except the back window on trucks & vans. <BR>I had a cop hassle me about my sail panels being to dark he had to stick his head in the car to make sure they were not windows.  ||||reg||1
Z||000011||fiero56||10-03-2000||04:40 PM||||The way the tinting percentages work(at least the way I understand it)is the higher the precentage the more light is allowed to pass through.<BR>5% allows 5% of light to pass through. 20% allows 20%... I would like to have been able to find 12-15%, think it would be perfect, 20% allows a little too much light to pass through for my taste. <P>I bought "Ultra Shield" tint film by Gila. Supposed to be the most scratch resistant available. Also blocks 99.4% of UV, and blocks 55% heat. Most tints probably have UV and heat blockage properties though. Total cost for both door glass was $25(2'x6.5'), and about an hour of my time.||||reg||1
Z||000012||DjKid||10-04-2000||01:18 AM||||My personal experince has been the only windows a cop can say anything about is the driverside front, and passenger side front, and windshield...  if ya look at  Blazers..  the rear windows on the 4doors are almost black..   the back windows cops can't, I wont say can't, cannot legally say anything about. However, even if you painted the rear window black, you do have to have a working rear view mirror. Thats what I was told. If anyone wants, I can ask my neighbor, a local city cop(also my cousins husband) about it. I'm sure he could tell me.<P>------------------<BR>Ray - Blue 88 Coupe - <A HREF="http://blueknight.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank>My Blue Knight</A> - <A HREF="http://www.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank> Carolina Fieros</A>||||reg||1
